# Network Security Group (NSG) Structure and Rules

## 1. Introduction

A Network Security Group (NSG) is an Azure networking resource used to filter inbound and outbound network traffic.

An NSG contains security rules that determine whether traffic should be:

- Allowed
- Denied

NSGs can be associated with:

- Network interfaces
- Subnets

